  "description": "One process of a swarm of worker processes. The library reads the process's configuration at start-up - a single line of JSON on standard input, or a file named on the command line when the process is started by hand - subscribes to the swarm's coordinator with the token it was given, and then runs the work the consuming application supplies until that work finishes, the coordinator ends it, the host member that started it goes away, or the coordinator stays out of reach too long. It always runs the application's shutdown step and exits with a documented code that says which of those happened. Pair it with CodeBrix.Swarm.Queen and CodeBrix.Swarm.Hive, and install all three at the same version.",
